---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base>
  <section class="page">
    <h1>Mission Statement</h1>
    <p>
      We nurture a personal relationship with Jesus Christ, feed spiritual hungers, heal spiritual wounds, and meet the deep human need for community. 
      Together we celebrate the faith and hope we share, form people in the Catholic Christian faith, and equip them for ministry. 
      Above all, we proclaim the Good News that God loves each of us unconditionally, forgives all our sins, and frees us from death.
    </p>

    <h3 class="history-subtitle">A Foundation of Faith Since 1957</h3>
    <div class="history-block">
      <img 
        class="reverend-photo" 
        src="/images/fr-firko.jpg" 
        alt="Rev. Clement Firko, founding pastor of Christ the King" 
      />
      <p>
        Christ the King Catholic Parish was established in 1956 under the leadership of its founding pastor, Reverend Clement Firko. 
        With a commitment to building a strong Catholic community, Father Firko brought parishioners together to construct a new church and rectory. 
        The first Mass in the new building was celebrated on March 31, 1957, and the church was officially dedicated by Bishop Joseph Clement Willging on October 27, 1957.
      </p>
      <p>
        Built with the support and dedication of its founding families, Christ the King began with approximately 400 families. 
        The parish quickly became a center of faith and fellowship, developing religious education programs, parish organizations, and community activities. 
        In 1965, a parish school was established to further the mission of Catholic education.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h3 class="history-subtitle">Growing Through the Years</h3>
    <p>
      Throughout the decades, Christ the King has been shaped by the dedication of its pastors, religious educators, staff, and parishioners. 
      Each generation has contributed to the spiritual life and growth of the parish through worship, education, service, and fellowship.
    </p>
    <p>Pastors, associate pastors, and deacons who have served our parish:</p>

    <h4>Pastors</h4>
    <ul class="clergy-list">
      <li><span>1957 — 1967</span> Fr. Clement Firko</li>
      <li><span>1967 — 1976</span> Msgr. Howard Delaney</li>
      <li><span>1977 — 1985</span> Fr. Delbert Blong</li>
      <li><span>1985 — 1995</span> Fr. William Gleeson</li>
      <li><span>1995 — 2014</span> Msgr. Tom Adrians</li>
      <li><span>2014 — 2017</span> Fr. Michael Papesh</li>
      <li><span>2017 — 2021</span> Fr. John Ozella</li>
      <li><span>2021 — 2024</span> Fr. Carl Wertin</li>
      <li><span>2024 — present</span> Fr. Zaldy Norba</li>
    </ul>

    <h4>Associate Pastors</h4>
    <ul class="clergy-list">
      <li><span>1960 — 1961</span> Fr. Charles Horne</li>
      <li><span>1962</span> Fr. John Power</li>
      <li><span>1966</span> Fr. Frederic Dean</li>
      <li><span>1967</span> Fr. Daniel Maio</li>
      <li><span>1969 — 1971</span> Fr. Frederic Dean</li>
      <li><span>1973 — 1975</span> Fr. Louis Stovik</li>
      <li><span>1977 — 1983</span> Fr. Michael Kurz</li>
      <li><span>1984 — 1985</span> Fr. Michael McCleary</li>
      <li><span>1985 — 1987</span> Fr. Nathanael Foshage, OSB</li>
      <li><span>1988 — 1989</span> Fr. James Moran</li>
    </ul>

    <h4>Deacons</h4>
    <ul class="clergy-list">
      <li><span>1995 — 2001</span> Deacon Phil Reynolds</li>
      <li><span>2002 — 2009</span> Deacon Michael LaConte</li>
      <li><span>2006 — 2007</span> Deacon Jake Arellano</li>
      <li><span>2010 — 2011</span> Deacon Darrell Pagels</li>
      <li><span>2011 — 2019</span> Deacon Steve Escalera</li>
      <li><span>2017 — 2023</span> Deacon Corey Compton</li>
      <li><span>2021 — present</span> Deacon John Chavez</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="history-subtitle">Continuing Our Mission</h3>
    <div class="history-block">
      <img 
        class="reverend-photo" 
        src="/images/fr-norba.jpg" 
        alt="Rev. Zaldy Norba, current pastor of Christ the King" 
      />
      <p>
        Today, Christ the King continues the mission entrusted to it by generations of faithful parishioners. 
        Under the leadership of Reverend Zaldy Norba, who became the parish's ninth pastor in August 2024, the community remains dedicated to growing in faith, celebrating the sacraments, and sharing the love of Christ.
      </p>
      <p>
        What began as a community of 400 families has grown into a parish of more than 600 registered families. 
        While the parish has changed throughout the years, its foundation remains the same: a community united in Christ and called to serve Him and one another.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .history {
    text-align: left;
    color: var(--gold);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--gold);
    padding-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .history-subtitle {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--blue);
    font-size: 1.3rem;
  }

  .reverend-photo {
    float: left;
    width: 180px;
    height: auto;
    margin: 0 1.25rem 0.75rem 0;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  .history-block::after {
    content: "";
    display: table;
    clear: both;
  }

  .clergy-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 0;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .clergy-list li {
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .clergy-list span {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 140px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--blue);
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .reverend-photo {
      float: none;
      display: block;
      margin: 0 auto 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>